e=\"-translate-x-1/2 -translate-y-1/2 [word-break:break-word] absolute flex flex-col font-['Outfit:SemiBold'] font-semibold h-[58px] justify-center leading-[0] left-[185px] text-[17px] text-[color:var(--parkey-text-on-action,white)] text-center top-[29px] w-[370px]\" data-node-id=\"249:6180\">\n          <p className=\"leading-[1.21]\">Send Reset Link</p>\n        </div>\n      </a>\n      <a className=\"-translate-x-1/2 -translate-y-1/2 [word-break:break-word] absolute cursor-pointer flex flex-col font-['Outfit:SemiBold'] font-semibold h-[46px] justify-center leading-[0] left-[213.3px] text-[16px] text-[color:var(--parkey-action-primary,#840561)] text-center top-[759.8px] w-[367px]\" data-node-id=\"249:6181\">\n        <p className=\"leading-[1.21]\">Back to Sign In</p>\n      </a>\n      <div className=\"-translate-x-1/2 -translate-y-1/2 [word-break:break-word] absolute flex flex-col font-['Outfit:Regular'] font-normal h-[55px] justify-center leading-[0] left-[214.3px] text-[12px] text-[color:var(--parkey-text-secondary,#d9cfde)] text-center top-[831.3px] w-[359px]\" data-node-id=\"249:6182\">\n        <p className=\"leading-[1.21]\">For privacy, Parkey does not reveal whether an account exists.</p>\n      </div>\n      <div className=\"absolute backdrop-blur-[20px] bg-[#20162e] h-[44px] left-[24.8px] right-[27.8px] top-[-1.2px]\" data-node-id=\"249:6183\" data-name=\"iOS Status Bar / Components\">\n        <div className=\"absolute inset-[31.82%_80.37%_27.27%_5.31%] overflow-clip\" data-node-id=\"I249:6183;126:7890\" data-name=\"Action\">\n          <p className=\"-translate-x-1/2 [word-break:break-word] absolute font-['SF_Pro_Text:Semibold'] leading-[normal] left-[27px] not-italic text-[15px] text-center text-white top-[calc(50%-9px)] tracking-[-0.165px] w-[54px]\" data-node-id=\"I249:6183;126:7891\">\n            9:41\n          </p>\n        </div>\n        <div className=\"-translate-y-1/2 absolute h-[14px] overflow-clip right-[14px] top-[calc(50%+1px)] w-[68px]\" data-node-id=\"I249:6183;126:7892\" data-name=\"Container\">\n          <SFSymbol>{`Image(systemName: \"battery.100percent\")`}</SFSymbol>\n          <div className=\"absolute inset-[11.43%_74.12%_12.14%_0.74%]\" data-node-id=\"I249:6183;126:7894\" data-name=\"Signal\">\n            <img alt=\"\" className=\"absolute block inset-0 max-w-none size-full\" src={imgSignal} />\n          </div>\n          <SFSymbol>{`Image(systemName: \"wifi\")`}</SFSymbol>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      <div className=\"absolute h-[34px] left-[25.8px] right-[26.8px] top-[881.8px]\" data-node-id=\"249:6184\" data-name=\"iOS Home Indicator / Components\">\n        <div className=\"-translate-x-1/2 absolute bg-white bottom-[8px] h-[5px] left-[calc(50%+0.5px)] rounded-[100px] w-[134px]\" data-node-id=\"I249:6184;126:2469\" data-name=\"Home Indicator\" />\n      </div>\n      <button className=\"absolute bg-[rgba(0,0,0,0)] block cursor-pointer left-[13.8px] size-[48px] top-[48.8px]\" data-node-id=\"249:6185\" data-name=\"Parkey / Shared Back\">\n        <div className=\"absolute left-[12px] size-[24px] top-[12px]\" data-node-id=\"I249:6185;243:5478\" data-name=\"Chevron left / teal\">\n          <img alt=\"\" className=\"absolute block inset-0 max-w-none size-full\" src={imgChevronLeftTeal} />\n        </div>\n      </button>\n    </div>\n  );\n}\nSUPER CRITICAL: The generated React+Tailwind code MUST be converted to match the target project's technology stack and styling system.\n1. Analyze the target codebase to identify: technology stack, styling approach, component patterns, and design tokens\n2. Convert React syntax to the target framework/library\n3. Transform all Tailwind classes to the target styling system while preserving exact visual design\n4. Follow the project's existing patterns and conventions\nDO NOT install any Tailwind as a dependency unless the user instructs you to do so.\n\nNode ids have been added to the code as data attributes, e.g. `data-node-id=\"1:2\"`.\nThese styles are contained in the design: Frosted Glass: Effect(type: BACKGROUND_BLUR, radius: 40).\nComponent descriptions: The following components have usage descriptions or documentation links defined in Figma. These descriptions provide important context about the intended usage, best practices, and any constraints for each component. Follow these guidelines when implementing or using these components.\n\n## Parkey / Icon / Email\n**Node ID:** 226:2952\n\nParkey reusable Email icon. Brand graphics are provider-specific.\n\n## Parkey / Navigation / Back\n**Node ID:** 243:5477\n\nCanonical Parkey back control: 48 × 48 px invisible touch target, teal chevron centered at (12,12), positioned at x=15 y=50 within a 430×932 screen. Apply navigation reactions to the INSTANCE, not the master. Use on all screen-level top-left back actions; no Back on top-level app home/splash.\nThe generated code contains image and SVG URL constants, e.g. const image = `${assetPathPrefix}/<asset file name>`, where assetPathPrefix is declared once at the top of the code and every asset URL interpolates it. These URLs are temporary download sources and expire after 7 days. Download each asset into the project with curl -L, then replace its URL in the generated code with a reference to the downloaded asset. Never use the temporary URLs as runtime image sources."
